{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And he said, Here now, etc. O Adonai, perhaps, etc.</b> He sought that HaShem shield on behalf of twenty, and the merit of Abraham on behalf of ten, as in his preceding request. And he did not say ״אַל יִחַר״ as he said when he asked if thirty be found — for they are more than twenty — for the reason that he added nothing in his prayer to shield by merit beyond what he asked before. Therefore he was precise in saying <b>אֶל אֲדֹנָי</b>, meaning that his prayer was on account of the shielding of the Master, blessed be He, that He shield on behalf of twenty."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:13.645050504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}